42	        // addressLine1 or a non-blank flat address — so earlier minimal (flat) owners stay accepted.
43	        // The normalized values replace the submitted ones, so they are what get stored, returned
44	        // and (via the composed 'address') compared; the composed 'address' is the normalized
45	        // addressLine1 with the normalized addressLine2 appended after a single space when present.
